File: JBatt
Version: 1.3
Author: Janne.Jalkanen@iki.fi


INTRODUCTION
------------

Have you ever wanted to see how much power your Psion uses? Want to know
how  much  the  Serial  Link  *really* eats your precious battery power?
Would you like to see this shown also in beautiful graphics?

Well, apart from the beautiful part, JBatt does exactly this.  It  wakes
up  at  settable  intervals (default is 5 seconds) and reports the power
usage during the last interval, drawing a nice, scrolling graph  of  it,
too.  You can use this to find bad programs that take away your precious
mAhs from your Psions power source, or just to use as a replacement  for
the System screen 'Battery Usage' menu item.

This is definitely a  no-thrills  and  no-frills  program,  it  is  only
4.1Kbytes  in  size  and is really my first OPL program, so be kind. Bug
reports would be nice, if anyone can find any bugs.


DISTRIBUTION
------------

JBatt is Freeware, ie. you can spread it freely around, as long as  this
file is accompanied with the main OPA (and the resource file as well).

JBatt is (C) Janne Jalkanen 1998. I shall not be  held  responsible  for
any  and  all  damages  that  may  be caused to you, your computer, your
family, your friends or your enemies by this program. You want security,
you buy commercial software!


COMPATIBILITY
-------------

JBatt was written on a 1 MB Siena, but theoretically should  work  on  a
Series  3a and 3c as well. However, since I do not possess a PC I cannot
test this on the 3a emulator and thus  I  would  be  quite  grateful  if
someone told me how it works on a 3a or 3c.

JBatt takes approximately 12 kB of memory while running.


INSTALLATION
------------

1. Copy JBATT.OPA to your APP directory.
2. If you do not already have it, make a directory in your root dir
   called "HLP"
3. Copy JBATT.RSC to the HLP directory.


USAGE
-----

JBatt is quite easy to use, since it really does not do much. In the top
half  of the screen you see interesting info about the battery status on
your Psion and in the lower half you see a window which is updated every
few seconds or so and it shows the average battery usage during the last
period.

You can set the screen update (and average consumption  period)  in  the
Preferences  menu  item.  If  you  set it to zero, then JBatt will use a
period a bit less than a second (see the power consumption rise...). The
maximum time allowed is 16min 49 s (999 seconds).

The battery voltages are shown also in the screen, but  they  should  be
taken with a grain of salt, as your Psion does not really have a voltage
meter inside. However, if the voltage drops below a  'good'  level,  the
voltage  will be shown in inverse. This is the same as the system screen
informing about a "Low battery".

The graph has in the right-hand border  a  scale,  which  contains  tick
marks every 10 mA. You may set the maximum value to be displayed on this
graph from the Preferences menu.

I don't suggest you use a very low value for the update interval, as the
battery  usage  of  your  Psion  will increase when the interval is very
short, because JBatt will be run more often. You can see it quite easily
in the graph ;-)

To switch to  a  smaller display,  use the 'Info' key  (Fn+Menu  on  the
Siena).  This will bring out the status window on the right hand side of
the screen.


