KNOWN BUGS AND FEATURES
-----------------------

- You can force an update of the screen by pressing any key.  I am not
  sure whether this is a good or a bad thing, so I let it stay.


HISTORY
-------

v1.0, 7-Jun-97
- First public release.

v1.1, 24-Jun-97
- JBatt can now be killed from the system screen, thanks to some example
  code by Alasdair Manson of Psion.  Thanks!
- JBatt couldn't handle battery changes.  Now it should detect them
  and update the display accordingly.

v1.2, 30-May-98
- Bug fix: If the computer was running on external power, the program
  crashed due to an overflow condition if it was on for more than 99
  hours.  Well, duh.  Reported by Raymond from UK.

v1.3, 21-Sep-98
- Added a new preferences option so that those people running on S3
  class machines can set the defaults correct for their machine.
- Added possibility to use a smaller screen (i.e. to show the info
  window on the side.






